---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base
  title="Best bank reconciliation automation tools for bookkeepers — Booke AI vs Digits vs Double vs Xenett"
  description="Four ways accounting firms automate bank reconciliation for QBO and Xero clients: Booke AI, Digits, Double and Xenett. What each automates, pricing verified Oct 2026, cost at 20 clients."
>
  <h1>Automate bank reconciliation: 4 tools compared</h1>
  <p>Bank rec is where month-end close stalls: unmatched lines, uncategorized transactions and balances that don't tie out. The tools below take different parts of that job off your plate. Some match transactions for you, one replaces the ledger, and one reviews the result. Directory entries only — not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Tool</th>
        <th>What it automates</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</th>
        <th>Best fit</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/booke-ai`}>Booke AI</a></td>
        <td>Works inside your existing ledger: automates daily bank reconciliation in Xero and daily bank-feed categorization in QBO; document matching and reconciliation prep</td>
        <td>Business $129/business/mo; firm plans by quote</td>
        <td>Firms keeping clients on QBO or Xero that want matching done before review</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/digits`}>Digits</a></td>
        <td>AI-native general ledger that matches activity against the ledger and reconciles accounts continuously; bank statements pull in automatically</td>
        <td>Per client: Essentials $65, Core $100, Pro $250 per month (US only)</td>
        <td>New or US clients you're willing to move off QBO/Xero onto a new ledger</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/double`}>Double (formerly Keeper)</a></td>
        <td>Close layer on top of QBO: AI transaction handling and reconciliations, with review focused on exceptions and close tracking across clients</td>
        <td>Per-client plans; no public prices, demo required</td>
        <td>QBO firms that want rec plus close status for every client in one place</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/xenett`}>Xenett</a></td>
        <td>Review, not matching: 50+ AI checks flag reconciliation discrepancies and errors; Close view shows reconciliation status; Inter-company Rec add-on auto-matches transactions across related entities</td>
        <td>AI Financials Review $7.50/client/mo; Workflow $10/client/mo; Inter-company Rec add-on $10/client/mo</td>
        <td>Firms that already reconcile in QBO/Xero and want a check before sign-off</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Pick by where the bottleneck is</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hours spent matching bank lines in Xero:</strong> Booke AI, which runs the daily Xero bank reconciliation.</li>
    <li><strong>You'd rather the ledger reconcile itself:</strong> Digits, but it replaces QBO/Xero and is US only.</li>
    <li><strong>Many QBO clients and no view of who's reconciled:</strong> Double, for rec plus close tracking per client.</li>
    <li><strong>Recs get done but errors slip through review:</strong> Xenett as a cheap review layer on top.</li>
    <li><strong>Related entities with inter-company balances:</strong> Xenett's Inter-company Rec add-on.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cost at 20 clients (list prices, monthly)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Xenett AI Financials Review: 20 × $7.50 = $150 (review only; you still reconcile).</li>
    <li>Digits Essentials: 20 × $65 = $1,300 (includes the ledger itself).</li>
    <li>Booke AI Business: 20 × $129 = $2,580 at the per-business price; firm plans are by quote.</li>
    <li>Double: not listed; ask for a quote.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/compare/uncategorized-transactions-tools`}>Uncategorized transactions tools</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/missing-receipts-tools`}>Missing receipts tools</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/docyt-vs-digits-vs-truewind`}>Docyt vs Digits vs Truewind</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/category/month-end-close`}>All month-end close tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
